#
#     git apply docs/graphify-index-wording.patch
#
# WHY (verified 2026-09-01, after the first graphify build in this repo):
#
# 1. Rule 1 said "No graphs are stored in this pipeline repo." That sentence is now literally false:
#    a `graphify-out/` index exists here. It is not a violation — this repo is graphed as its own
#    client (the `self` workspace of rule 2), so its graph living in its own checkout, gitignored and
#    read by path, IS the client-repo pattern rule 1 describes. What the rule actually protects is
#    (a) never COMMITTING a graph and (b) never turning this repo into a central store of other
#    repos' graphs. The new wording states those two guarantees directly instead of a blanket claim
#    that the working tree now contradicts. Verified: `git ls-files graphify-out/` = 0 tracked files;
#    `git check-ignore -v graphify-out/graph.json` -> .gitignore:56.
#
# 2. Rule 1's sources carve-out path was stale after the zone restructure — it read
#    `users/<user>/workspaces/<workspace>/sources/cache/`, missing the `zones/<zone>/` segment that
#    rule 2 mandates. The runtime is already zoned: `WorkspaceStore` carries `_zone` and Z4 deleted
#    the legacy 3-level `zone=None` path, so the prose was the only thing behind.
#
# 3. The .gitignore header carried the same now-false "Nothing graph-related is stored here."
#
# Behaviour-neutral: prose only, no code and no ignore-rule changes (`graphify-out/` on line 56 is
# untouched and still the only thing preventing a 16 MB index from being committed — note that CI and
# scripts/check-no-content.sh contain zero graphify references, so that one line is the sole guard).
#
# NOT covered by this patch (reported separately, needs its own pass): the same pre-zone
# `workspaces/<client>/` and `users/<user>/workspaces/<workspace>/` wording still appears in several
# module docstrings — pipeline/store.py (lines ~3, 41, 58, 125, 188, 209, 218, 402, 422) and
# pipeline/sources/cache.py (line ~38).
